From: Isabella Basso <isabellabdoamaral@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:13:54 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] joystick: Forward custom effects to combined controller children

The combined Joy-Con driver rejects HD Rumble packets even though both
child drivers accept them. Forward each effect to both devices and report
failure if either child rejects it. Always attempt both writes.

---
 src/joystick/hidapi/SDL_hidapi_combined.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/joystick/hidapi/SDL_hidapi_combined.c b/src/joystick/hidapi/SDL_hidapi_combined.c
--- a/src/joystick/hidapi/SDL_hidapi_combined.c
+++ b/src/joystick/hidapi/SDL_hidapi_combined.c
@@ -162,7 +162,16 @@

 static bool HIDAPI_DriverCombined_SendJoystickEffect(SDL_HIDAPI_Device *device, SDL_Joystick *joystick, const void *data, int size)
 {
-    return SDL_Unsupported();
+    int i;
+    bool result = true;
+
+    for (i = 0; i < device->num_children; ++i) {
+        SDL_HIDAPI_Device *child = device->children[i];
+        if (!child->driver->SendJoystickEffect(child, joystick, data, size)) {
+            result = false;
+        }
+    }
+    return result;
 }

 static bool HIDAPI_DriverCombined_SetJoystickSensorsEnabled(SDL_HIDAPI_Device *device, SDL_Joystick *joystick, bool enabled)
